import WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck

/-!
# Forward-space automaton certificate for Starknet's Poseidon permutation

Data and kernel checks for the middle bound of `WideTrail.Poseidon.StarknetMiddle`. The
partial-round matrix is `M = [[3, 1, 1], [1, -1, 1], [1, 1, -2]]` (`mdsMatrix` of
`WideTrail.Poseidon.Starknet`), which is `diag (2, -2, -3) + J`, over `ZMod p` with
`p = fieldModulus` (the value of `Poseidon.Starknet.modulus`, the STARK prime); the S-box of a
partial round is on coordinate `2`, and the window is the `83` partial rounds. The same matrix is
the linear layer of the full rounds.

* `mdsRows`: the matrix `M`, row `i` holding the coefficients of output coordinate `i`, with `-1`
  and `-2` written as `p - 1` and `p - 2`. `mdsDiagonal`: the array `d = (2, -2, -3)` with
  `M = diag d + J` (`mdsDiag`), with `-2` and `-3` written as `p - 2` and `p - 3`.
* `states`: a forward-space automaton (`Hades.AutomatonCheck.AState`) with `84` states. State `0`
  has no functional (it stands for every difference), potential `2` and depth `0`. For `k ≥ 1`,
  state `k` has depth `k` and stands for the differences on which its functionals vanish (one
  for odd `k`, two for even `k`): a subspace that contains every difference with which a trail
  whose first `k` rounds are inactive, inactive, active, inactive, active, … can enter round `k`.
  Its potential is `1` for odd `k` and `0` for even `k`. For the states of depth less than `83`:
  an active round leads from `0` and from every odd state to state `0`, and from an even state
  `k ≥ 2` to state `k + 1`; an inactive round leads from `0` to `1` and from an odd state `k` to
  `k + 1`, and is impossible from an even state `k ≥ 2`.
* `trailStates`, `trailSboxOutputs`: a trail through the `91` rounds of the Starknet schedule (`4`
  full rounds, `83` partial rounds with the S-box at coordinate `2`, `4` full rounds, the matrix
  `M` in every round): row `n` of `trailStates` is the difference entering round `n`, row `n` of
  `trailSboxOutputs` the difference after its S-box layer.
* `middleStates`, `middleOutputs`: rows `4, …, 87` of `trailStates` and coordinate `2` of rows
  `4, …, 86` of `trailSboxOutputs`, read as a trail through the `83` partial rounds.

The checks, each by `decide +kernel`:

* `automaton_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkAll` passes for the window of `83` rounds with
  `mdsRows`, the S-box at coordinate `2` and start state `0`; `start_pot`: the start state has
  potential `2`, so the certificate gives `(83 + 1 - 2) / 2 = 41`.
* `trail_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkHadesTrail` passes for the `4 + 83 + 4` rounds;
  `trail_weight`: the charged weight of that trail is `57`.
* `middle_trail_check`: `Hades.RelationCheck.checkTrail` passes for `middleStates` and
  `middleOutputs` with `mdsDiagonal`, over the `83` partial rounds.

The data were computed outside Lean from the literals of the instance file (`mdsMatrix` and
`mdsDiag` of `WideTrail.Poseidon.Starknet`); nothing depends on how they were found, since the
checks are complete. This file imports only `WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck`, which imports only
`WideTrail.Hades.RelationCheck` and through it `Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic`.

## What is not claimed

The checks are statements about lists of natural numbers. What they mean for trails is proved in
`WideTrail.Hades.Automaton` and `WideTrail.Hades.WindowRelation`, and applied in
`WideTrail.Poseidon.StarknetMiddle` and `WideTrail.Poseidon.Checks.StarknetMiddle`. The witness
trail is a trail in the `IsTrail` model (supports, masks and linear maps only); it is not claimed
to be realised by an input pair or a key.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Poseidon.Certificates.Starknet

open Hades.AutomatonCheck (AState)

